      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — meaningful variable names, named constants, and a clarifying comment about the expected output.I made an error replacing the null characters with spaces. I need to restore the exact expected string from the original.I still used spaces instead of null characters. Let me fix this with the exact original expected string.I keep writing actual null bytes instead of the `\\u0000` escape sequences. Let me write the file correctly with literal escape sequences.Let me check the compile script to understand the Java version and classpath.Java 8 doesn't have `String.repeat()`. I'll build the expected string with `new String(new char[211])` instead, avoiding the long unreadable literal.Now let me compile-check the test."
